DevSecOps in Production

🔐 DevSecOps in Production — A Real-Time Pipeline Guide Nobody Talks About in Enough Detail
If you're building software and shipping it to production without security baked into every step, you're gambling with your systems.

Here's the exact production-grade DevSecOps pipeline I use — 8 stages, 6 tools, running in real time with GitLab triggering Jenkins. Let me walk you through every step so you can implement it today. 👇

🏗️ The Pipeline Overview

GitLab → [Build & Unit Test] → [Code Coverage] → [SCA] → [SAST]
       → [Quality Gates] → [Build Image] → [Scan Image] → [Smoke Test] → 📧 Notification.

Every stage has a specific tool. Every tool has a job. Nothing ships unless the pipeline is green.

🔧 Stage 1 — Build & Unit Test | Maven
✅ Compiles code & runs tests
🔌 Plugin: Maven Integration Plugin
Why it matters: If the code doesn't build or tests fail, there's zero point running security scans. Fail fast, fix fast.

Stage 2 — Code Coverage | JaCoCo
✅ Measures test coverage %
🔌 Plugin: JaCoCo Plugin
Why it matters: High test coverage = lower risk of shipping bugs. JaCoCo gives you hard numbers, not guesses.

Stage 3 — SCA | OWASP Dependency Check
✅ Scans 3rd-party libs for CVEs
🔌 Plugin: OWASP Dependency-Check Plugin
Why it matters: Log4Shell happened because of an unchecked dependency. SCA makes sure you're not unknowingly shipping known exploits.

Stage 4 — SAST | SonarQube
✅ Static code analysis — finds bugs, secrets & vulnerabilities
🔌 Plugin: SonarQube Scanner for Jenkins
Why it matters: SAST catches vulnerabilities before the code even runs — it's your first line of code defense.

Stage 5 — Quality Gate | SonarQube
✅ Hard stop — pipeline fails if standards aren't met
🔌 Same SonarQube plugin + configure threshold in SonarQube UI
Why it matters: This is your automated code reviewer. No human approval needed — the gate enforces standards automatically.

Stage 6 — Build Image | Dockerfile + Docker
✅ Containerizes the app
🔌 Plugin: Docker Pipeline Plugin
Why it matters: "It works on my machine" is dead. Containers ensure your app runs identically from dev to prod.

Stage 7 — Scan Image | Aqua Trivy
✅ Scans Docker image for OS CVEs & misconfigs
🔌 No plugin needed — install via: apt-get install trivy
Why it matters: A clean source code doesn't mean a clean image. Base images carry their own CVEs — Trivy catches them before they hit production.

Stage 8 — Smoke Test
✅ Validates app is alive in staging
🔌 Use curl: curl -f http://staging:8080/health || exit 1
Notification | Email Extension Plugin
✅ Alerts team on every build result.
Why it matters: Every pipeline run should notify your team — success or failure. No surprises in production.

💬 Final 
Security is not a checkbox at the end of sprint. It's a pipeline.
Build it once. Let it run forever. Sleep better at night. 
